# How these values are used
# ---------------------------
# `make build` (or `go generate ./backend/internal/secrets` from the repo root)
# embeds the keys below that are marked [embedded] into the binary, so the
# packaged app needs no .env at runtime. They are sealed with AES-256-GCM and a
# per-build key split into masked shares: this is OBFUSCATION (it defeats
# `strings`/grep), not protection against someone who reverse-engineers the
# binary. The generated file (backend/internal/secrets/secrets_gen.go) is
# gitignored; a build without .env simply embeds nothing.
# At runtime, an environment variable or a .env in the current directory
# always overrides the embedded value (handy for development).
# NSONLINE_ENV_FILE=path/to/other.env   # read by the generator instead of ./.env (e.g. in CI)

# Discord applications (https://discord.com/developers/applications). [embedded]
# Discord shows the application NAME as the title ("Playing Nintendo Switch 2"),
# so create one app per console and name it after the console:
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID_SWITCH2=
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID_SWITCH=
# Fallback when the console has no dedicated app (also used by `nsonline rpc`):
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# Token cache file of login/me/friends/watch/serve (default: nso-auth.json). Contains
# your session token: never commit it. `nsonline setup`, `config` and `app` use the
# data dir instead (--data-dir, default: the desktop app's folder) and ignore it.
# NSO_AUTH_FILE=nso-auth.json

# --- Coral via nxapi-znca-api --- [embedded]
# Register a client at https://nxapi-auth.fancy.org.uk (scopes ca:gf ca:er ca:dr).
NXAPI_ZNCA_API_CLIENT_ID=
# Client authentication, one of (SECRET: never commit a filled .env):
#   client secret:
# NXAPI_ZNCA_API_CLIENT_SECRET=
#   shared secret ("Shared secret" on the client page; signs an HS256 client assertion):
# NXAPI_ZNCA_API_SHARED_SECRET=
# Contact URL or address added to our User-Agent, as the API terms ask: [embedded]
# NSONLINE_CONTACT=https://github.com/you/nsonline
# NSO app version to imitate (latest: https://nxapi-znca-api.fancy.org.uk/api/znca/config): [embedded]
# NSO_APP_VERSION=3.6.0

# --- watch ---
# Account whose presence goes to Discord (nsaId from `nsonline friends`, or its name):
# NSO_WATCH_FRIEND=
# Flags: -interval, -idle-interval, -friends-interval (serve): 15s by default, 15s minimum
# `serve` / `watch`: -show-idle shows an "Idle" activity while the console is on
# without a game (the desktop app has its own "showIdle" setting).

# --- language ---
# Language of the CLI and backend messages (CLI usage, prompts, Discord activity
# texts, API errors): en (default) or fr. Not secret. The `--lang <code>` flag
# overrides it; the desktop app sets it for the backend it launches.
# NSONLINE_LANG=en

# --- desktop app sidecar (`nsonline app --data-dir <dir>`) ---
# NSONLINE_API_TOKEN is set by the desktop app for the backend it launches (random,
# per launch, required, never on the command line). Do not put it in this file.
